from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(3,'english','thank-god','Thank God!',
 ('The farmer and the king','A Jataka tale tells of a farmer who grew many fruits and decided to gift the best ones to the king. He chose grapes because watermelons were too heavy to carry far. When the playful king threw grapes at him, the farmer kept saying Thank God. In this chapter you will read why, learn words that are opposites, use is and are correctly, and put a fruit salad recipe in order.'),
 [('The story begins',['A farmer who liked fruits decided to grow many kinds of fruit on his land.','With hard work and care, his trees grew well, and he took special care of grapes and watermelons in a small corner.','When the fruits were ripe, he wanted to gift the best fruit to the king.','His wife said that the best fruits that year were the watermelons and the grapes.','The journey to the palace was long and watermelons were too heavy, so the farmer put bunches of grapes in a basket and walked to the palace.']),
  ('At the palace',['The guard took the farmer to the royal garden, where the king was playing with the princess.','The farmer quietly put the basket in front of the king and sat down.','When the king rested, the guard brought him the basket and said it was a gift from the farmer.','The king was in a playful mood. He ate one grape and then threw another grape at the farmer.','The grape hit the farmer on the forehead, and the farmer said Thank God.']),
  ('Why did he say Thank God?',['The king was surprised and threw a grape again. Again the farmer said Thank God and called himself blessed.','The king asked why he was thanking God when grapes were being thrown at him.','The wise farmer smiled and explained that he had chosen the grapes over the watermelons.','If he had brought watermelons, they would have hurt much more. So he was thankful for a small trouble instead of a big one.','The story teaches us to look at the bright side and to be thankful.']),
  ('New words',['A journey is a trip from one place to another.','A guard protects a place and a royal garden is the garden of a king.','Popped means put something quickly into the mouth. Wise means clever and sensible.','Sight words like grow, kept, front and again are words you should recognise at once when reading.']),
  ('Opposites',['Words that have the opposite meaning are called opposites. Heavy is the opposite of light.','A thick book is opposed by a thin book. A long journey is opposed by a short journey.','Soft cotton is opposed by hard rock, and a slow tortoise by a fast rabbit.','Other pairs are hot and cold, big and small, up and down.']),
  ('Is and are',['We use is when we speak about one thing and are when we speak about more than one.','The table is made of wood, because there is one table.','These mangoes are sweet, because there are many mangoes.','The toys are on the shelf, but the book is on the table. I is not used with is, we say I am.']),
  ('Listen, speak and write',['A funny poem tells of an elephant with a mighty cold who needs a handkerchief the size of a bed sheet.','If you visit a sick elephant, you could take fruits, warm soup or tulsi tea, and say them aloud.','Chandu mixed up the steps of making a fruit salad. First he takes banana slices, next papaya cubes, then apple slices, then grapes, then he mixes them, and finally he squeezes lemon with a pinch of salt.','The word search has fruits such as mango, papaya, grapes, banana, guava, plum, peach and pear.'])],
 [('Write the opposite of the underlined word: a long journey.',[('Look at the underlined word: long.','Long tells the length of the journey.'),('The opposite of long is short.','Opposites have the opposite meaning.'),('So the phrase is a short journey.','Check that it makes sense.')]),
  ('Fill in is or are: The girls ___ at the shop.',[('Girls means more than one.','More than one needs are.'),('So we write: The girls are at the shop.','For one girl we would write: The girl is at the shop.')]),
  ('Put in order: A. Then I mix them all. B. First I take banana slices. C. Finally I squeeze a lemon.',[('The first step has the word first: B.','First starts the recipe.'),('Then comes mixing: A.','Mixing is done after adding the fruits.'),('Finally comes the lemon: C. The order is B, A, C.','Words like first, then and finally show the order.')])],
 ('Tell the story of the farmer and the king and explain why the farmer said Thank God.',['The farmer took grapes as a gift','The king threw grapes at him','Watermelons would have hurt more','Be thankful and look at the bright side'],['The farmer was angry','The king threw watermelons','The farmer did not bring a gift']),
 ['The farmer gifted grapes because watermelons were too heavy.','He said Thank God because grapes hurt less than watermelons.','Opposites have opposite meanings: heavy and light.','Use is for one and are for more than one.','Words like first, next and finally show the order of steps.'],
 [M('1',1,'What did the farmer grow on his farm?','Fruits',[('Rice','He grew fruits'),('Flowers','The story is about fruits')],'He grew many kinds of fruits.'),
  M('2',1,'Why did the farmer take grapes to the king?','Watermelons were too heavy to carry',[('He did not like watermelons','The reason was weight'),('The king hated watermelons','Nothing like that is said')],'The journey was long and watermelons are heavy.'),
  M('3',1,'What did the king do playfully?','He threw grapes at the farmer',[('He ate all the grapes','He threw them'),('He gave the farmer gold','Not in the story')],'He threw a grape at the farmer.'),
  M('4',1,'Why did the farmer say Thank God?','Watermelons would have hurt more',[('He liked grapes thrown at him','He was thankful it was not worse'),('He was afraid','He was smiling')],'He was glad he had not brought watermelons.'),
  M('5',2,'What is the opposite of heavy?','Light',[('Big','Big is not the opposite'),('Hard','Hard is not the opposite')],'Heavy and light are opposites.'),
  M('6',2,'What is the opposite of slow?','Fast',[('Soft','Not the opposite'),('Long','Not the opposite')],'A slow tortoise and a fast rabbit.'),
  M('7',2,'Fill in the blank: These mangoes ___ sweet.','are',[('is','Mangoes means many'),('am','Am goes with I')],'Many things need are.'),
  M('8',2,'Fill in the blank: The table ___ made of wood.','is',[('are','One table needs is'),('be','Not used here')],'One thing needs is.'),
  F('9',2,'The farmer chose watermelons for the king.',False,'He chose grapes.'),
  M('10',2,'Which fruit is in the word search?','Papaya',[('Carrot','Carrot is a vegetable'),('Potato','Potato is a vegetable')],'Papaya is a fruit in the grid.'),
  S('11',2,'What kind of tale is this story?',['jataka tale','a jataka tale','jataka'],'It is a Jataka tale.'),
  M('12',3,'What does the story teach?','Be thankful and look at the bright side',[('Always bring watermelons','The farmer was lucky he did not'),('Never visit a king','The story is not about that')],'The farmer was thankful for a smaller trouble.')],
 keep=['Jataka','journey'])
